\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Vertices placed on the circle}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{\ref{fdip-0096} gives a distance between vertices of a
directed cycle: the least number of edges joining them.
Dividing by the number #{N} of vertices puts a neighboring
pair at distance #{1/N}. The point #{j/N} on the circle of
length #{1} reproduces those distances as arc length. The
image is finite. How far is that finite set from the whole
circle?}
